        "original_id": "f61b1af3-adfe-5692-b8d1-184de71e580e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alison Castle, Linda McCartney, Paul McCartney\n- Companies: Taschen, TASCHEN, The Beatles\n- Products: The Stanley Kubrick Archives, Linda McCartney's Life in Photography, Some Like It Hot, Kubrick's Napoleon: The Greatest Movie Never Made, Marc Newson: Works, Saturday Night Live: The Book\n- Roles: photographer, book editor, musician, animal rights activist, entrepreneur, publisher\n\nFacts:\n- Linda McCartney was born as Linda Louise Eastman on September 24, 1941, and she was later known as Lady McCartney.\n- Linda McCartney was an American musician, photographer, animal rights activist, entrepreneur, and publisher.\n- Linda McCartney was married to Paul McCartney of the Beatles.\n- Linda McCartney died on April 17, 1998.\n- Alison Castle is an American photographer and book editor.\n- Alison Castle prominently worked on The Stanley Kubrick Archives for Taschen.\n- Alison Castle edited Linda McCartney's Life in Photography, Some Like It Hot, Kubrick's Napoleon: The Greatest Movie Never Made, Marc Newson: Works, and Saturday Night Live: The Book, all published by TASCHEN.",
